#
# Counter-example for the native math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds gate: a
# math:ProbabilityValue whose math:quantityValue magnitude (1.5) lies outside the
# closed unit interval [0, 1], so the native probability gate MUST emit
# math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds (and no other probability failure class). It carries a
# gmeow:hasReferenceFrame so math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape (P3) stays SATISFIED,
# isolating exactly the out-of-bounds range gate rather than also tripping the
# unframed-value shape.
# Back-reference: math:ProbabilityValue / math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:outOfBoundsProbability a math:ProbabilityValue ;
    math:quantityValue "1.5" ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:outOfBoundsFrame .

ex:outOfBoundsFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/outOfBoundsProbability> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
